# Apple (Australia) components

Restate intent: marketing UI that is token-driven, consistent, and fast to implement.

Every interactive component must define default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, and error. Do not ship guidance or UI without those states.

## Density (apple.com/au reference)

Prefer link-led pages, then buttons and lists. Inputs, global nav, and tables are rare.

| Kind | Count on reference | Implication |
|------|-------------------|-------------|
| links | 321 | Default navigation pattern; descriptive labels |
| buttons | 74 | Primary CTAs use `surface.muted` + inverse text |
| lists | 60 | Group related offers/features |
| inputs | 2 | Forms stay short |
| navigation | 2 | One global + one utility/footer |
| tables | 2 | Use only for comparable specs |

## Anatomy and tokens

- Spacing and type must use `space.*` and `font.size.*` only.
- Pill CTAs should use `radius.xs` or `radius.sm` (full pill).
- Motion should use `motion.duration.instant` (feedback), `fast` (hover), `normal` (panels).

## Interactions (must document all three)

- Keyboard: Tab/Shift+Tab move focus; Enter/Space activate buttons; Escape closes overlays; arrows in menus.
- Pointer: hover does not replace focus-visible; click target should stay at least the control’s padding box.
- Touch: no hover-only affordances; hit area should not shrink below the padded control.

## Responsive and edge cases (must)

- Long content: wrap; do not truncate essential labels without a title/accessible name.
- Overflow: clip decorative media; keep actions visible (wrap or stack).
- Empty: one sentence + one labeled action; no ambiguous “OK”/“Click here”.
- Loading: disable duplicate submits; keep accessible name; expose busy state.
- Error: message associated with the control; recovery action labeled.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button style={{ color: '#0066cc', padding: '13px' }}>Click here</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="btn-primary" aria-busy={loading} disabled={loading || disabled}>
  {loading ? 'Saving…' : 'Save resume'}
</button>
```
